  "html": "<table class=\"toc\" id=\"toc\" summary=\"Contents\"><tr><td><div id=\"toctitle\"><h2>Contents</h2></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1\"><a href=\"#White_Paladin\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">White Paladin</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2\"><a href=\"#Skills\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Skills</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2\"><a href=\"#Equipment\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Equipment</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2\"><a href=\"#Strategy.2FTactics\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Strategy/Tactics</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2\"><a href=\"#Advantages\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Advantages</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2\"><a href=\"#Disadvantages\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Disadvantages</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2\"><a href=\"#How_do_you_know_if_you_have_enough_endurance_as_a_fighter.3F.21\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">How do you know if you have enough endurance as a fighter?!</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</td></tr></table>\n<a name=\"White_Paladin\"></a><h1> <span class=\"mw-headline\">White Paladin</span></h1>\n<p>A Paladin is basically a pure fighter with Divine skills.  It can be a very effective build and is fun to play. Essentially the idea of this build is to get rid of the \"Barbarian\" skills Butcher and Cleave, and replace them with Divine skills.  It takes a bit of time to acquire all the Divine skills, but by Level 20 you will have a fearsome build. \n</p><p><br/>\n</p>\n<a name=\"Skills\"></a><h2> <span class=\"mw-headline\">Skills</span></h2>\n<table>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/Gym-freak.png\" title=\"Image:Gym-freak.jpg\"><img alt=\"Image:Gym-freak.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"43\" src=\"/images/recovered/Gym-freak.png\" width=\"43\"/></a>\n</td><td><b><a href=\"/wiki/Gym_Freak\" title=\"Gym Freak\">Gym Freak</a></b> is the standard fighter Passive skill.\n</td><td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/Way-of-the-roo.png\" title=\"Image:Way-of-the-roo.jpg\"><img alt=\"Image:Way-of-the-roo.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"43\" src=\"/images/recovered/Way-of-the-roo.png\" width=\"43\"/></a>\n</td><td><b><a href=\"/wiki/Way_of_the_Roo\" title=\"Way of the Roo\">Way of the Roo</a></b> is the other fighter Passive.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/Righteous-stomp.png\" title=\"image:Righteous-stomp.jpg\"><img alt=\"image:Righteous-stomp.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"43\" src=\"/images/recovered/Righteous-stomp.png\" width=\"43\"/></a>\n</td><td><b><a href=\"/wiki/Righteous_Stomp\" title=\"Righteous Stomp\">Righteous Stomp</a></b> is a beginning Divine skill.\n</td><td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/Soul-rend.png\" title=\"image:Soul-rend.jpg\"><img alt=\"image:Soul-rend.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"43\" src=\"/images/recovered/Soul-rend.png\" width=\"43\"/></a>\n</td><td><b><a href=\"/wiki/Soul_Rend\" title=\"Soul Rend\">Soul Rend</a></b> is the basic Divine damage skill at L5.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/Fear-of-gosh.png\" title=\"Image:Fear-of-gosh.jpg\"><img alt=\"Image:Fear-of-gosh.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"43\" src=\"/images/recovered/Fear-of-gosh.png\" width=\"43\"/></a>\n</td><td><b><a href=\"/wiki/Fear_of_Gosh\" title=\"Fear of Gosh\">Fear of Gosh</a></b> can be useful against groups of fodder at L14.\n</td><td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/Holy-roller.png\" title=\"image:Holy-roller.jpg\"><img alt=\"image:Holy-roller.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"43\" src=\"/images/recovered/Holy-roller.png\" width=\"43\"/></a>\n</td><td><b><a href=\"/wiki/Holy_Roller\" title=\"Holy Roller\">Holy Roller</a></b>  is a great Divine damage skill at L20.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/Divine-ascendancy.png\" title=\"Image:Divine-ascendancy.jpg\"><img alt=\"Image:Divine-ascendancy.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"43\" src=\"/images/recovered/Divine-ascendancy.png\" width=\"43\"/></a>\n</td><td><b><a href=\"/wiki/Divine_Ascendancy\" title=\"Divine Ascendancy\">Divine Ascendancy</a></b> is the buff to all your Divine attacks at L12.\n</td><td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/1h-swivel-arm-action.png\" title=\"image:1h-swivel-arm-action.jpg\"><img alt=\"image:1h-swivel-arm-action.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"43\" src=\"/images/recovered/1h-swivel-arm-action.png\" width=\"43\"/></a>\n</td><td><b>Swivel Arm Action <a href=\"/wiki/1H_Swivel_Arm_Action\" title=\"1H Swivel Arm Action\">1H</a> or <a href=\"/wiki/2H_Swivel_Arm_Action\" title=\"2H Swivel Arm Action\">2H</a></b> is a useful buff at L5.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/Shadow-lightning.png\" title=\"image:Shadow-lightning.jpg\"><img alt=\"image:Shadow-lightning.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"43\" src=\"/images/recovered/Shadow-lightning.png\" width=\"43\"/></a>\n</td><td><b><a href=\"/wiki/Shadow_Lightning\" title=\"Shadow Lightning\">Shadow Lightning</a></b> makes up for the lack of a Divine AoE skill at L3.\n</td><td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/I.png'm_Rubber_You're_Screwed.jpg\" title=\"image:I'm Rubber You're Screwed.jpg\"><img alt=\"image:I'm Rubber You're Screwed.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"43\" src=\"/images/recovered/I.png'm_Rubber_You're_Screwed.jpg\" width=\"43\"/></a>\n</td><td><b><a href=\"/wiki/I'm_Rubber,_You're_Screwed\" title=\"I'm Rubber, You're Screwed\">I'm Rubber, You're Screwed</a></b> works very well if you use a shield at L25.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/Poison-resistance.png\" title=\"Image:Poison-resistance.jpg\"><img alt=\"Image:Poison-resistance.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"43\" src=\"/images/recovered/Poison-resistance.png\" width=\"43\"/></a>\n</td><td><b>Resistances</b> can be added as needed.\n</td><td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/Bling-gnome.png\" title=\"Image:Bling-gnome.jpg\"><img alt=\"Image:Bling-gnome.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"43\" src=\"/images/recovered/Bling-gnome.png\" width=\"43\"/></a>\n</td><td><b><a href=\"/wiki/Bling_Gnome\" title=\"Bling Gnome\">Bling Gnome</a></b> rounds out the package for members.\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p><br/>\nAt higher levels, you can add:<br/>\n</p>\n<table>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/My-flaming-buddy.png\" title=\"image:My-flaming-buddy.jpg\"><img alt=\"image:My-flaming-buddy.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"43\" src=\"/images/recovered/My-flaming-buddy.png\" width=\"43\"/></a>\n</td><td><b><a href=\"/wiki/My_Flaming_Buddy\" title=\"My Flaming Buddy\">My Flaming Buddy</a></b> is not a Divine skill, but it works very well<br/> for a Paladin once you reach Level 50.\n</td><td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/Ray-of-gosh.png\" title=\"image:Ray-of-gosh.jpg\"><img alt=\"image:Ray-of-gosh.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"43\" src=\"/images/recovered/Ray-of-gosh.png\" width=\"43\"/></a>\n</td><td><b><a class=\"missing\" href=\"/wiki/Ray_of_Gosh\" title=\"Ray of Gosh\">Ray of Gosh</a></b> is great once you are at Level 45.\n</td></tr></table>\n<p>Obviously, there are more Divine skills than you can fit in your skills tray at one time.  Part of the fun of playing this build is adjusting the skills to suit your current situation.\n</p>\n<a name=\"Equipment\"></a><h2> <span class=\"mw-headline\">Equipment</span></h2>\n<table>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/Body-_Ornate_Plate_64px.png\" title=\"Image:Body- Ornate Plate 64px.jpg\"><img alt=\"Image:Body- Ornate Plate 64px.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"128\" src=\"/images/recovered/Body-_Ornate_Plate_64px.png\" width=\"64\"/></a>\n</td><td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/Boots-_Ornate_Greaves_64px.png\" title=\"Image:Boots-_Ornate_Greaves_64px.jpg\"><img alt=\"Image:Boots-_Ornate_Greaves_64px.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"64\" src=\"/images/recovered/Boots-_Ornate_Greaves_64px.png\" width=\"64\"/></a><br/><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/Gloves-_Ornate_Gauntlets_64px.png\" title=\"Image:Gloves-_Ornate_Gauntlets_64px.jpg\"><img alt=\"Image:Gloves-_Ornate_Gauntlets_64px.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"64\" src=\"/images/recovered/Gloves-_Ornate_Gauntlets_64px.png\" width=\"64\"/></a>\n</td><td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/Helm-_Ornate_Helm_64px.png\" title=\"Image:Helm-_Ornate_Helm_64px.jpg\"><img alt=\"Image:Helm-_Ornate_Helm_64px.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"64\" src=\"/images/recovered/Helm-_Ornate_Helm_64px.png\" width=\"64\"/></a><br/><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/Shoulders-_Ornate_Spaulders_64px.png\" title=\"Image:Shoulders-_Ornate_Spaulders_64px.jpg\"><img alt=\"Image:Shoulders-_Ornate_Spaulders_64px.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"64\" src=\"/images/recovered/Shoulders-_Ornate_Spaulders_64px.png\" width=\"64\"/></a>\n</td><td>Obviously, a Paladin COULD choose any type of fighter armor.  However, prompted by vanity and a sense of appropriateness, I chose to wear Ornate Plate at low levels.\n</td></tr>\n<table>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/Body-_Sunstone_Armor.png\" title=\"Image:Body- Sunstone Armor.jpg\"><img alt=\"Image:Body- Sunstone Armor.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"128\" src=\"/images/recovered/Body-_Sunstone_Armor.png\" width=\"64\"/></a>\n</td><td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/Boots-_Sunstone_Boots_64px.png\" title=\"Image:Boots-_Sunstone_Boots_64px.jpg\"><img alt=\"Image:Boots-_Sunstone_Boots_64px.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"64\" src=\"/images/recovered/Boots-_Sunstone_Boots_64px.png\" width=\"64\"/></a><br/><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/Gloves-_Sunstone_Gauntlets.png\" title=\"Image:Gloves-_Sunstone_Gauntlets.jpg\"><img alt=\"Image:Gloves-_Sunstone_Gauntlets.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"64\" src=\"/images/recovered/Gloves-_Sunstone_Gauntlets.png\" width=\"64\"/></a>\n</td><td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/Helm-_Sunstone_Helm_64px.png\" title=\"Image:Helm-_Sunstone Helm_64px.jpg\"><img alt=\"Image:Helm-_Sunstone Helm_64px.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"64\" src=\"/images/recovered/Helm-_Sunstone_Helm_64px.png\" width=\"64\"/></a><br/><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/Shoulder-_Sunstone_Spaulders_64px.png\" title=\"Image:Shoulder-_Sunstone_Spaulders_64px.jpg\"><img alt=\"Image:Shoulder-_Sunstone_Spaulders_64px.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"64\" src=\"/images/recovered/Shoulder-_Sunstone_Spaulders_64px.png\" width=\"64\"/></a>\n</td><td>Visiting the Amazon frequently allowed me to accumulate a beautiful set of Sunstone armor and by Level 50 I was clad as a shining Paladin!  Most Unique Sunstone pieces include a +Divine damage so it is perfect for a Paladin.  Finding Jewelry with +Divine is harder but it is available.\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n<table>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/1h-weapon-_Reliance.png\" title=\"1h-weapon- Reliance.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" border=\"0\" height=\"96\" src=\"/images/recovered/1h-weapon-_Reliance.png\" width=\"64\"/></a>\n</td><td><a href=\"/wiki/Reliance\" title=\"Reliance\">Reliance</a> is a Mythic weapon that looks great for a Paladin and gives a lot of +Divine. There is also a Unique version.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/1h-weapon_Wrath.png\" title=\"1h-weapon Wrath.jpg\"><img alt=\"\" border=\"0\" height=\"96\" src=\"/images/recovered/1h-weapon_Wrath.png\" width=\"64\"/></a>\n</td><td><a href=\"/wiki/Wrath\" title=\"Wrath\">Wrath</a> is another great Mythic weapon for a Paladin.  Soul Sword is the Unique version.\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"image\" href=\"/images/recovered/1h-Weapon-_Sword_of_Gosh.png\" title=\"image:1h-Weapon-_Sword_of_Gosh.jpg\"><img alt=\"image:1h-Weapon-_Sword_of_Gosh.jpg\" border=\"0\" height=\"96\" src=\"/images/recovered/1h-Weapon-_Sword_of_Gosh.png\" width=\"32\"/></a>\n</td><td>Probably the ultimate Paladin Mythic weapon is <a href=\"/wiki/Not_the_Sword_of_Gosh\" title=\"Not the Sword of Gosh\">Not the Sword of Gosh</a> with lots of Divine bonus!\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n<p><br/>\n</p>\n<a name=\"Strategy.2FTactics\"></a><h2> <span class=\"mw-headline\">Strategy/Tactics</span></h2>\n<p>The Paladin is a very versatile build.  The various Divine skills are acquired gradually so you can experiment with one and then move on to the next.  Righteous Stomp, the starting skill, is very useful for the <a href=\"/wiki/Whisker_Broodling\" title=\"Whisker Broodling\">Whisker Broodlings</a> in <a href=\"/wiki/Dew_Valley_Forest\" title=\"Dew Valley Forest\">Dew Valley Forest</a>.  Then, just as you need it for the <a href=\"/wiki/Whisker_Blademaster\" title=\"Whisker Blademaster\">Whisker Blademasters</a> and <a href=\"/wiki/Dew_Valley_Rattle_Tooth\" title=\"Dew Valley Rattle Tooth\">Dew Valley Rattle Tooth</a> you can get Soul Rend.  Fear of Gosh is next and can be a difficult skill to learn to use properly, but very effective.  When you get Holy Roller at L20 you are ready to function as a full fledged Paladin.\n</p><p>A group of mobs that includes some big guys is effectively dealt with by first rushing the biggest with Holy Roller and then hitting him with Soul Rend.  Fodder can be trashed with Fear of Gosh followed by Righteous Stomp.  Picking the right skills and arranging them properly on your buttons is a challenge and adds interest to the build.\n</p>\n<a name=\"Advantages\"></a><h2> <span class=\"mw-headline\">Advantages</span></h2>\n<ul><li>By concentrating on Divine skills, you make Divine Ascendency a principal asset and buff up almost everything you do.\n</li></ul>\n<ul><li>The Paladin plays very much like a standard Tank and can be an effective \"meat shield\" in groups.\n</li></ul>\n<a name=\"Disadvantages\"></a><h2> <span class=\"mw-headline\">Disadvantages</span></h2>\n<ul><li>You have to spread points into INT which can slightly limit your STR and AGI.  Achieving a good balance is critical.\n</li></ul>\n<ul><li>If you allow vanity to rule, the Ornate Plate does not have as high a DEF as Crystal or Amethyst Plate.  However it has some very nice bonuses available.\n</li></ul>\n<a name=\"How_do_you_know_if_you_have_enough_endurance_as_a_fighter.3F.21\"></a><h2> <span class=\"mw-headline\">How do you know if you have enough endurance as a fighter?!</span></h2>\n<ul><li>An easy equation that helps with all classes is this, (level/100)*24000. This gives you a final number that is one of the most accurate ways of telling you if you have enough endurance. But then, it depends on you're build.. what skills you use.. etc.\n</li></ul>\n<p>Say I was a level 30 fighter. I have only 7000 health. Using the equation - (30/100)*24000 - I get a total of 7200. This means the suggested amount of health I should have is 7200. And I have 7000, so I am okay for how much I have. Then again, this is only a suggested amount, and you can just use it as a basis for everything else. \n</p>\n<ul><li> Note!: This formula does not apply to BSoL mages! As they don't need much health, as they rely on a good supply of mana to keep them going.\n</li></ul>\n</table>\n\n \n<div class=\"visualClear\"></div>"
}
